At 12:58 PM 03/20/2001 -0500, Robin Lee Powell wrote:
>Am I the _only_ person here who doesn't believe in this whole 'objective
>reality' thing?  Or, at least, that no human being can percieve
>'objective reality', even if it does exist?

Lojban supports you then.  Use jetnu for subjective truth that is observer 
independent given a common epistemology, and djuno for subjective truth 
that is observer dependent (this seems to be where others don't necessarily 
agree with me because they don't like subjective truth to be called 
"knowledge", but you can always weaken the claim by using belief as your 
epistemology).  fatci is the word for objective truth.

